  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>GLM - Poisson Exponential Family</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The probability mass function for the Poisson distribution is given by:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; {@lambda_var@}) = \frac{e^{-{@lambda_var@}} {@lambda_var@}^y}{y!} \]</p>
<p>Show that this belongs to the exponential family by rewriting it in the form:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; \theta) = a(\theta)b(y) \exp(yQ(\theta)) \]</p>
<p>Identify the following components in terms of \({@lambda_var@}\):</p>
<p>\(Q({@lambda_var@}) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(a({@lambda_var@}) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(b(y) = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>What is the <strong>canonical link function</strong> \(g(\mu)\)?</p>
<p>\(g(\mu) = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Rewrite the pmf:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; {@lambda_var@}) = \frac{e^{-{@lambda_var@}} {@lambda_var@}^y}{y!} \]</p>
<p>\[ = e^{-{@lambda_var@}} \cdot \frac{1}{y!} \cdot e^{\log({@lambda_var@}^y)} \]</p>
<p>\[ = e^{-{@lambda_var@}} \cdot \frac{1}{y!} \cdot e^{y \log({@lambda_var@})} \]</p>
<p>Matching \( f(y; \theta) = a(\theta)b(y) \exp(yQ(\theta)) \):</p>
<p>\[ Q({@lambda_var@}) = \log({@lambda_var@}) \]</p>
<p>\[ a({@lambda_var@}) = e^{-{@lambda_var@}} \]</p>
<p>\[ b(y) = \frac{1}{y!} \]</p>
<p>The canonical parameter is \(\theta = \log({@lambda_var@})\). Since \(\mu = E[Y] = {@lambda_var@}\), the canonical link function is:</p>
<p>\[ g(\mu) = \log(\mu) \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
