  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>GLM - Normal Exponential Family</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The probability density function for a Normal distribution with known variance \(\sigma^2\) is:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; {@mu_var@}) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} \exp\left( -\frac{(y - {@mu_var@})^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \]</p>
<p>Show that this belongs to the exponential family by rewriting it in the form:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; \theta) = a(\theta)b(y) \exp(yQ(\theta)) \]</p>
<p>Identify the following components in terms of \({@mu_var@}\) and \(\sigma\):</p>
<p>\(Q({@mu_var@}) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(a({@mu_var@}) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(b(y) = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Expand the exponent:</p>
<p>\[ -\frac{(y - {@mu_var@})^2}{2\sigma^2} = -\frac{y^2 - 2y{@mu_var@} + {@mu_var@}^2}{2\sigma^2} = -\frac{y^2}{2\sigma^2} + \frac{y{@mu_var@}}{\sigma^2} - \frac{{@mu_var@}^2}{2\sigma^2} \]</p>
<p>Rewrite the pdf:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; {@mu_var@}) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} \exp\left( -\frac{y^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \exp\left( \frac{y{@mu_var@}}{\sigma^2} - \frac{{@mu_var@}^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \]</p>
<p>\[ = \left[ \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} \exp\left( -\frac{{@mu_var@}^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \right] \cdot \left[ \exp\left( -\frac{y^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \right] \cdot \exp\left( y \frac{{@mu_var@}}{\sigma^2} \right) \]</p>
<p>Matching \( f(y; \theta) = a(\theta)b(y) \exp(yQ(\theta)) \):</p>
<p>\[ Q({@mu_var@}) = \frac{{@mu_var@}}{\sigma^2} \]</p>
<p>\[ a({@mu_var@}) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} \exp\left( -\frac{{@mu_var@}^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \]</p>
<p>\[ b(y) = \exp\left( -\frac{y^2}{2\sigma^2} \right) \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
